**Branch** : feature/GTP-21

**created endpoints as** :
         POST /api/applications — creates a new application in Draft status for the authenticated user
         POST /api/applications/{id}/submit — transitions a Draft application to Submitted and records the submission timestamp
         On successful submission, an ApplicationSubmittedEvent is published via the IEventPublisher abstraction

**Sample Test Cases**
**Create Draft Application 
Endpoint: POST /api/v1/applications**
**Request Body:**
```c#
{
  "programId": 1
}
``` 
**Expected Response — 201 Created:**
```c#
{
  "applicationId": 101,
  "programId": 1,
  "applicantId": 5,
  "status": "Draft",
}
```

**Submit a Draft Application
Endpoint: POST /api/v1/applications/101/submit**
Expected Response — 200 OK:
```C#
{
  "applicationId": 101,
  "programId": 1,
  "applicantId": 5,
  "status": "Submitted",
  "submittedDate": "2026-04-07T10:05:00Z"
}
```
Submit Non-Existent Application
**Endpoint: POST /api/v1/applications/9999/submit**
Expected Response — 404 Not Found:
```c#
{
  "error": "Application not found."
}
```
**Submit an Already-Submitted Application**
Endpoint: POST /api/v1/applications/101/submit
Expected Response — 409 Conflict:
```c#
{
  "error": "Only Draft applications can be submitted."
}
```
 **Non-Applicant Role Attempts to Create Application**
Endpoint: POST /api/v1/applications
Expected Response — 403 Forbidden:
```c#
{
  "error": "You do not have permission to perform this action."
}
```
**Request Without Authentication Token**
Endpoint: POST /api/v1/applications
Expected Response — 401 Unauthorized:
```c#
{
  "status": 401,
  "title": "Unauthorized",
  "type": "https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc9110#section-15.5.2"
}
```